local-12: spread decodes over the PP microbatches (V2 + PP + async scheduling)

With PP microbatching a request may decode only every pp_size steps
(next_decode_eligible_step). Decodes scheduled in the same step therefore stay
in the same microbatch forever: two requests that start together share one
microbatch and two of the three stages idle. Measured on Swift Flash-Next PP=3,
MTP n=2, 2 streams x 800 tokens: started together ~102 t/s total (51 + 51),
started 0.4-1.5 s apart 148-164 t/s (75-83 each). This caps the decodes taken
per step at ceil(running decodes / pp_size), so with 2 decodes each step takes
one and they settle into separate microbatches. Prefill chunks are not capped.
VLLM_PP_DECODE_SPREAD=0 restores the old behavior. Not upstream (no open PR).
Scheduler unit tests: same 2 pre-existing PP-config failures, no new ones.

